WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.417
A correlated subquery uses a value from the current outer row.

00:00:04.417 --> 00:00:09.052
For example, the outer query may define patients as p.

00:00:09.052 --> 00:00:15.357
Inside the subquery, a condition may compare a child patient ID with p patient ID.

00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:20.757
When the outer patient changes, the inner query's matching value changes too.

00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:25.807
This is why correlated subqueries are useful for per-row calculations.

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:30.472
A correlated subquery refers to the current row of the outer query.

00:00:30.472 --> 00:00:35.857
Conceptually, the inner query is evaluated in relation to each outer row.

00:00:35.857 --> 00:00:41.237
That makes some business rules easy to express, but it can be expensive at scale.

00:00:41.237 --> 00:00:46.462
Compare a correlated formulation with a pre-aggregated join when performance matters.
